For every performed Infinity, an '''Infinity (∞)''' is gained. This number boosts some Infinity upgrades. (1;1, 5;2, 6;2, 12;1, 16;1-2 and 17;1)

Upgrade 18;1 makes the Infinity count go up passively.

== Generators ==
Generator 1 (G1) generates '''Generator Power''' (GP). To begin with GP is powered to 0.666, but this can be improved with Infinity Upgrades (14;2, 19;1 and 20;2).

GP multiplies Mult Gain. (e.g. If GP is 16, it is powered to 0.666, meaning the mult gain mult is 16 divided by the cube root of 16, which equals ~6.35, and now if you used to get 30 Red Mult per Red revolution, now you get ~190.)

Generator 2 (G2) generates G1, Generator 3 (G3) generates G2, G4 generates G3 and so on.

Buying Generators multiplies its interval by 2x.

Generator Mult is softcapped at 1e1,000.

==Infinity Challenges==
Challenges are unlocked when you buy Infinity Upgrade '''7;1'''. Each challenge has a handicap that you will need to overcome.

The goal is to Infinite with the corresponding handicap (see table below).

Each completed challenge:

* Grants a challenge-specific bonus
* Adds +1 to IP gain multiplier
