Challenges 4 and 9 may take several hours. Others normally take under 1 hour.

After all 9 challenges are completed, you will have the option to '''Break Infinity.'''

==Break Infinity==
After completing all 9 challenges, you can break or fix Infinity in the Challenges tab.

Upon reaching e3,080 score, the 10x IP bar will fill up. Every e308 increase in score will 10x the IP gain for your current run.

=== Challenge Times ===
Infinity challenges, once completed, will have an amount of time shown below every challenge. This is the best time achieved on this challenge (during this Eternity). These times should be brought down as much as possible because certain Infinity Upgrades get '''better''' with '''lower challenge times''' (15;2-4, 16;3 and 17;2). Aptly named Infinity upgrade 19;3 is really useful for this purpose. (Infinity Upgrades 15;2-4, 16;3 and 17;2 are only useful after all Infinity challenges have been completed at least once.)

'''NOTE:''' Once challenges get instantly completed upon entry, make sure they're done WITHOUT Time Flux, because the time calculation is multiplied by your Time Flux speed up (e.g. If a challenge was completed with a time of 200ms while 2x game speed is enabled, if it was completed without Time Flux, the time would be 100ms). This difference is marginal with higher times.

== Stars ==
Stars are unlocked with Infinity Upgrade 21;1. They are the last tab in this prestige layer.

The mechanics are straightforward and involve generating Stardust with Stars, which enhances Generators and Generator Power gain. The price of Stars increases significantly with each purchase, starting at 1e33 (1 Dc), these first increase by 1e3 each time, but later start increasing by 1e7 or more.

When unlocking Stars, It's recommended to '''save up 2e33 (2 Dc) IP''' in order to buy both Infinity Upgrade 21;1 and your first Star.

Stars can be upgraded by:

* Buying Stars
* Increasing Star Base (Each purchase increases it by 0.275, starting at 2.75) (Formula: 2.75 + 0.275 * n  where n is number of purchases)
* Increasing Star Exponent (Each purchase increases it by 0.05, starting at 0.4) (Formula 0.4 + 0.05 * n  where n is number of purchases)

Stars and Star Upgrades should be prioritized '''over Generators'''.

Stardust can be spent on '''Stardust Upgrades''', of which there are 4:

# Infinity Upgrade 1;1 applies to: G1 (with every purchase the next Generator is added, '''this upgrade is the strongest'''. Maxed out at G10)
# Infinity Gain (Increases by +1x for every purchase. This upgrade can be bought an unlimited number of times)
# Upgrade 2;1 Exp. Box Power (Increases by 0.01 with every purchase. Maxed out at +0.5)
# Upgrade 18;1 is 1.05x faster (Maxes out at x62.62)

Every Stardust Upgrade should be bought immediately when available. Stardust is reset to zero each Infinity, so it's worth checking if you can buy any Stardust Upgrades before you Infinite.

For more information about Stars, you can refer to the [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1912_7kvYPpKxBt95xHBcCADIdYWUeycI8JZbueDpO5g/edit?usp=sharing stardust calculator] by angelamoureux.

As you progress, you'll approach the 1.79e308 IP milestone, allowing you to Eternate and enter the '''[[Eternity]]''' layer.

